If you don't want to write custom editor scripts from scratch, the popular, open-source **[NaughtyAttributes](https://github.com/dbrizov/NaughtyAttributes)** package provides a `[Foldout]` attribute that works just like a header.

1. Install it via Unity Package Manager (add git URL: `https://github.com/dbrizov/NaughtyAttributes.git#upm`).
2. Use `[Foldout]` instead of `[Header]`:

```csharp
using UnityEngine;
using NaughtyAttributes;

public class PlayerController : MonoBehaviour
{
    [Foldout("Movement Settings")]
    public float walkSpeed = 5f;

    [Foldout("Movement Settings")]
    public float sprintSpeed = 10f;

    [Foldout("Combat Settings")]
    public int health = 100;

    [Foldout("Combat Settings")]
    public int attackPower = 15;
}
```

