Here's a simple function that takes an array and a number of items per page as input and returns an array of paginated arrays:
```php
function paginateArray(array $array, int $itemsPerPage): array
{
    $pageNumber = (int) $_GET['page'] ?? 1;
    $offset = ($pageNumber - 1) * $itemsPerPage;

    $paginatedArray = array_slice($array, $offset, $itemsPerPage);

    return [
        'items' => $paginatedArray,
        'total_pages' => ceil(count($array) / $itemsPerPage),
        'current_page' => $pageNumber,
    ];
}
```
